render.prompt:
{style_spec}

MODULE SPEC:
{module_spec}

Generate the complete Python module implementing this spec, following the style contract above exactly — same docstring convention, same import ordering, same type-hint coverage, same error-handling shape, same naming conventions as the worked example.

Emit ONE path-bearing fence at {module_path}. After it, include ONE pathless bash fence containing exactly:
python3 -m py_compile {module_path}
No other commentary outside the fences.

compliance.prompt:
{style_spec}

MODULE SPEC:
{module_spec}

COMPILE CHECK OUTPUT:
{compile_output}

ACTUAL WRITTEN MODULE (the real file on disk, not a draft):
{written_module}

Compare the actual written module against the style contract and the module spec. List every deviation, one per line: missing/incorrect type hints, docstring convention violations, naming convention violations, import-order violations, an interface/signature mismatch from MODULE SPEC, or a failing compile check. If there are none, write exactly: NO ISSUES FOUND.

FINDINGS:
{style_findings}

Respond with exactly one word: PASS if FINDINGS is exactly "NO ISSUES FOUND", otherwise FAIL. No other text.

final.prompt:
{module_path} still has open style/spec deviations after revision:
{style_findings}

Review it directly, then either edit it by hand or re-run this workflow. Type ACK to end this run.
